{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1781615674,"nonce":"Mklk/Msm2rAJ72mOJq6GYILlT8U=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABFp9PMA","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/287","origin":"github"},"title":"BizzyBoat udp_bridge: audit + size queue_size across ALL bridged topics (fail-fresh under link saturation)","message":"## Summary\n\nAudit and deliberately size the per-topic `queue_size` (and the global\n`publish_queue_max_bytes`) across **all** bridged topics on BizzyBoat's\n`udp_bridge` config — not just the OAK camera streams. Prompted by the\n**2026-06-15 Massabesic survey (#277, PR #279)**, where messages arrived ~30 s\nlate while the Starlink uplink was saturated by the camera streams.\n\n## Why this is the right interim knob\n\n`udp_bridge` stamps each packet with a **send-time** timestamp + a monotonic\n`packet_number` *at wrap time* (`wrapped_packet.cpp:13`), and is type-generic so\nit never reads the inner ROS `header.stamp`. On the receive side there is **no\nage gate** before republish — the only receive-side dropping is `PublishQueue`\nevicting the **oldest when over a byte budget** (`udp_bridge.cpp:177`). So a late\nmessage is **republished as if current**.\n\nUntil the proper fixes land (see \"Relationship\" below), the cheapest lever is\nqueue depth: a **shallow queue makes the bridge \"fail fresh\" (drop the stale\nbacklog) instead of \"fail stale\" (deliver it 30 s late)** — the same instinct as\nAQM/CAKE (keep queues short). A 100-deep queue on a high-rate video topic can\nhold ~100 stale frames across a link stall; that is the staleness amplifier we\nwant to remove.\n\n## Current state (verified — `bizzyboat_project11/config/bizzyboat.yaml`, two `operator` connection blocks)\n\n- OAK ffmpeg + segmentation streams: `queue_size: 100`\n- Sidescan port/starboard/down: `queue_size: 50`\n- `tf`: `queue_size: 25` in connection block 1, **unset** in block 2 (inconsistent)\n- **Everything else has no explicit `queue_size`** → built-in default. This\n  includes the reliable/low-rate control + telemetry: `command_response`,\n  `diagnostics`, `heartbeat`, `collision_*` polygons/pointcloud/state, `odom`,\n  all `mavros_*` (gps/imu/position/velocity), `battery`, `plan`, `platforms`,\n  `tf_static`, `*_camera_info`, `sidescan_nadir_depth`, `water_temperature`, etc.\n- **`publish_queue_max_bytes` is not set anywhere** (boat or operator side) →\n  built-in default byte budget. Receiver side also lives in\n  `bizzyboat_project11/config/operator.yaml`.\n- Uneven throttle: OAK starboard/port carry `period: -1.0` (full rate) while\n  forward/aft do not specify `period` (ties to PR #279 review suggestion #6).\n\n## Proposed approach — classify, then size per class\n\nSize by **QoS reliability × rate**, not one global number:\n\n| Class | Topics | Queue policy |\n|---|---|---|\n| High-rate best-effort **bulk** | OAK ffmpeg video, OAK segmentation raw, sidescan images, watercolumn | **Shallow (1–2)** — fail-fresh; the big saturation win. Drop stale frames rather than buffer 100. |\n| Reliable **control / telemetry** | `command_response`, `heartbeat`, `mavros_*`, `collision_*`, `odom` | **Leave default / tune carefully.** Shallow + RELIABLE → the `ResendRequest` path re-delivers the dropped stale data. Do **not** aggressively shrink these. |\n| Low-rate / latched | `tf_static`, `platforms`, `plan`, `*_camera_info`, `received_global_plan` | depth 1 is fine; make `tf` consistent across both blocks. |\n| Global byte budget | (both ends) | set `publish_queue_max_bytes` deliberately rather than relying on the default. |\n\n## The catch to respect\n\nOn a **RELIABLE** connection, dropping at the queue triggers `udp_bridge`'s\nresend path, which re-delivers the very data you dropped (potentially stale).\nSo the shallow-queue mitigation is clean on **best-effort high-rate streams** and\n**counterproductive on reliable control** — tune accordingly, per topic.\n\n## Relationship to the real fixes (this is a band-aid, not a replacement)\n\n- **Transit-buffer staleness** (packets stuck in the Starlink/WireGuard buffer)\n  is **not** addressable by `udp_bridge` queues at all — that is the **CAKE /\n  network-stability** lane (separate issue).\n- The **correctness guarantee** (\"never republish something older than what I\n  already republished\") is the **monotonic-freshness receive gate** (separate\n  `udp_bridge` issue). Queue tuning only reduces the magnitude/probability of\n  staleness; it cannot detect it.\n\nThese three compose; none replaces the others.\n\n## Notes / acceptance\n\n- Params are read at configure/topic-setup → a **bridge restart** is needed for\n  changes to take effect (not a live `param set`).\n- Verify each topic's actual QoS (reliability) before shrinking — best-effort\n  vs reliable drives the policy.\n- Audit covers **both** connection blocks in `bizzyboat.yaml` and the receive\n  side in `operator.yaml`.\n- Drop the `period: -1.0` inconsistency on OAK starboard/port while here\n  (PR #279 review #6).\n\nPart of the #277 post-survey stability backlog.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}